ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the late 1980s The Netherlands Twin Register (NTR) was established by recruiting young twins and multiples at birth and by approaching adolescent and young adult twins through city councils.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17254420") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254420+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000125)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the multi-center ICGN study [22],[23] subjects with known COPD were recruited as probands, and siblings and available parents were ascertained through the probands.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19300482") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2650282/") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001899)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the phase 2 PANDA trial, patients with previously untreated resectable G/GEJ tumors (n = 21) received neoadjuvant treatment with one cycle of atezolizumab monotherapy followed by four cycles of atezolizumab plus docetaxel, oxaliplatin and capecitabine.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:38191613") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38191613+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000314)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the phase 2 adaptive BELLINI trial, patients with early-stage triple-negative breast cancer received neoadjuvant nivolumab with or without ipilimumab, showing immune activation, clearance of circulating tumor DNA and promising clinical response rates, especially in patients preselected based on high levels of tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:39284953") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11564107/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000224)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the population-based Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR) cohort, we sought to examine whether a decline in the prevalence and incidence of end-stage renal disease (ESRD) was evident with increasing calendar year of type 1 diabetes diagnosis among people followed for 25 years.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24026564") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898749/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000806)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present cross-sectional pilot study, the primary aim was to determine the feasibility of using prostate biopsy (PB) as a screening tool (irrespective of the PSA level) in men with a FH of PrCa.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:27151655") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4912360/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000080)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the prospective cohort GENEPSO, which aims at assessing environmental and lifestyle risk factors, BRCA1/2 mutation carriers are followed over time to observe characteristics of subjects who are developing either primary or secondary cancer.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:34325649") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8320036/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0002723)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the prospective cohort Health Effects of Arsenic Longitudinal Study (HEALS), trained physicians unaware of arsenic exposure interviewed in person and clinically assessed 11 746 population-based participants (aged 18-75 years) from Araihazar, Bangladesh.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20646756") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20646756+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000204)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this MAGIC effort, individuals without diabetes of self-reported and genetically clustered European (85%), African American (6%), South Asian (5%), East Asian (2%) and Hispanic (2%) ancestry from up to 64 cohorts participated.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:39280063") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000536)
