ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To date, 35 PIs from 28 research institutions have joined the effort, which now comprises summary level data for more than 70,000 patients and controls from 45 cohort studies.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "http://www.scallop-consortium.com/") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000398)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To date, over 7000 Amish adults have participated in one or more of our studies as part of the Amish Complex Disease Research Program72.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35393526") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000416)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To define host genetic effects on the outcome of a chronic viral infection, we performed genome-wide association analysis in a multiethnic cohort of HIV-1 controllers and progressors, and we analyzed the effects of individual amino acids within the classical human leukocyte antigen (HLA) proteins.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21051598") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3235490/") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000917)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To describe the design and ongoing conduct of the Million Veteran Program (MVP), as an observational cohort study and mega-biobank in the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) health care system.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26441289") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26441289+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000371)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To differentiate between the direct symptomatic effects and possible disease modifying effects of levodopa, we use a randomised delayed-start double-blind placebo-controlled multi-centre trial design.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26584951") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4653886/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001200)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To do so, we analyzed data from the population-based Jerusalem Lipid Research Clinic (LRC) cohort study which was initiated in the 1970s as a cardiovascular prevalence study, using protocols of the North American LRC prevalence studies [24–26].") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21220750") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3145913/") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001950)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To evaluate the safety of high-dose NR therapy, we conducted a single-center, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind, phase I trial on 20 individuals with PD, randomized 1:1 on NR 1500 mg twice daily (n = 10) or placebo (n = 10) for four weeks.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:38016950") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10684646/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0002739)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the genetic factors underlying familial glioma, the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium (GLIOGENE Consortium) was formed in 2006 to recruit families affected by ≥2 cases of glioma from 14 institutions across 5 countries (12).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26656478") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0002720)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To exploit the new molecular technologies, an international group of investigators from Australia, New Zealand and the UK have formed “The Aneurysm Consortium” and recently obtained funding to carry out a GWAS of AAA.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:18621558") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2697027/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0001463)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To fill this gap, the Mexican Biobank project genotyped 6,057 individuals from 898 rural and urban localities across all 32 states in Mexico at a resolution of 1.8 million genome-wide markers with linked complex trait and disease information creating a valuable nationwide genotype-phenotype database.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:37821706") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37821706+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000114)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To further characterize PCa’s genetic basis, we undertook a GWAS using multiple study cohorts within Kaiser Permanente (KP), a fully integrated health care delivery system: the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH) cohort (dbGaP phs000674.p1), the ProHealth Study, and the California Men’s Health Study (CMHS).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26034056") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000945)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To further investigate the relationship between menopausal hormones and risk of colon cancer, we conducted a population-based case-control study in Los Angeles County involving 831 women with newly diagnosed colon cancer and 755 population-based control women.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:20064828") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:20064828%20AND%20SRC:MED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000766)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To gain insight into the etiology of lung cancer among never-smoking women, we formed the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia (FLCCA), which includes studies drawn from mainland China, South Korea, Japan, Singapore, Taiwan, and Hong Kong.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23143601") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4169232/unicode") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000864)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To generate larger sample sizes for GWAS meta-analysis of asthma enabling the discovery of common novel risk loci, we established the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium (TAGC) across worldwide groups of investigators with genome-wide data available in >142,000 individuals of diverse ancestries.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:29273806") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5901974/") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0001419)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify Bipolar Disorder (BD) genetic susceptibility factors, we conducted two genome-wide association (GWA) studies: one involving a sample of individuals of European ancestry (EA; n = 1,001 cases; n = 1,033 controls) and one involving a sample of individuals of African ancestry (AA; n = 345 cases; n = 670 controls).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19488044") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3035981/") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001751)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify additional psoriasis susceptibility loci, we carried out a genome-wide association scan of 1,409 psoriasis cases and 1,436 controls in partnership with the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN)6 (see Table 1 and Supplementary Table 1 for details of case and control collections).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19169254") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2745122/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001152)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify the determinants of immune variability, the Milieu Intérieur (MI) population cohort study14 was established in 2012–2013, consisting of 1000 well-defined healthy donors equally stratified by age and sex (100 male and 100 female donors in each decade of life between 20 and 69 years old).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:42173848") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13354573/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000301)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate these associations, we conducted a multicenter case-control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx in nine countries.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:14652239") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14652239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0002212)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate this, the authors undertook a case-control study (n = 1,012) of the association between NSAIDs and more advanced prostate cancer in Ohio men recruited between 2001 and 2004 and evaluated whether this association was modified by a functional polymorphism in the lymphotoxin alpha (LTA) gene (LTA C+80A, where the CC genotype results in higher LTA production).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:16931544") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16931544+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001564)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To limit contamination by the presence of confounding factors such as cranial irradiation, a more homogenous subcohort of patients was selected for WP4b.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30888333") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000988)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To minimize selection bias, participants were drawn from extended pedigrees of Mexican American families recruited at random from the San Antonio, Texas community.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:36204553") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9531122/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001818)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To our best knowledge, the TMM BirThree Cohort Study is the first study to involve a birth and three-generation cohort from an initial stage of cohort construction combined with genome and omics analyses.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:31504573") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000939)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To provide a set of individuals to test the framework for GPSCAD assessment, a second set of individuals −1,826 CAD cases and 1,209 controls - were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals at 5 cities in India -- Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:32762905") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7592606/unicode") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0002051)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To reduce potential pathologic heterogeneity, the Autopsy-Confirmed Parkinson Disease Genetics Consortium (APDGC) collected a set of individuals with PD that have neuropathologic confirmation of Lewy body PD pathology, as well as a set of “autopsy-confirmed” control individuals with no evidence of PD neuropathology.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25663231") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0001055)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To robustly characterize these effects, we performed a genome-wide association study of 207 taxa and 205 pathways representing microbial composition and function in 7,738 participants of the Dutch Microbiome Project.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:35115690") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35115690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000059)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To search for common schizophrenia susceptibility variants, we carried out a GWAS in cases from three methodologically similar National Institute of Mental Health repository-based studies, and screened controls from the general population.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:19571809") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2775422/") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000116)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To study the genetics of asthma, a familial collection was built in the Saguenay-Lac-Saint-Jean (SLSJ) region, which is localized in northeastern Quebec, Canada, and which is characterized by a young founder effect.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:24646526") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24646526+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000000 coho:COHO_0000149)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To systematically profile the variation of the TME and to characterize biomarkers for diverse treatments, the integrated immunoprofiling of large adaptive cancer patient cohorts (IMMUcan) consortium acquires molecular and cellular profiles of over 2,500 patients across five cancer types up to 2026") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:40930089") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12539258/fullTextXML") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000278)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To systematically screen for age- and/or sex-specific effects of genetic variants on BMI and WHRadjBMI, we performed meta-analyses of 114 studies (up to 320,485 individuals of European descent) with genome-wide chip and/or Metabochip data by the Genetic Investigation of Anthropometric Traits (GIANT) Consortium.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26426971") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26426971+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") coho:COHO_0000001 coho:COHO_0000558)
